    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178-a1">

                <pb facs="0260" n="994" xml:id="pg994"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 75.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ransom to Mr. Mariscal and Mr. Leon.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to communicate to you that
                    I have received from my Government its approbation of the joint designation of
                    myself as arbitrator of the Governments of Mexico and Guatemala under the
                    convention of these two countries of the 1st of April, 1895, and that it will
                    give me very great pleasure to accept that high trust.</p>
                <p>I am deeply sensible of the distinguished honor conferred upon me as the
                    representative of the United States by this appointment, coming from sister and
                    neighboring Republics, and it will be my constant endeavor to pursue and render
                    equal and impartial justice to both.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">M. W. Ransom.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
